# Demonstrates the optional backpressure feature's 503 response (specs/003-ingestion-backpressure).
# Only reachable when BACKPRESSURE_ENABLED=true and the service is currently at capacity —
# with the default (disabled) configuration, this batch is simply accepted (200).
#
# To reproduce locally:
#   BACKPRESSURE_ENABLED=true BACKPRESSURE_MAX_PENDING_ROWS=1 docker compose up --build -d
# then fire this request concurrently with itself (or any other POST /logs traffic) a few
# times in quick succession — one of the concurrent requests should land while the other
# is still admitted-but-not-completed.

### May return 200 (accepted) or 503 (temporarily at capacity), depending on concurrent load
POST http://localhost:8080/logs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "logs": [
    {
      "timestamp": "2026-07-20T14:32:01.123Z",
      "level": "info",
      "service": "backpressure-demo",
      "message": "may be shed under load",
      "attributes": {}
    }
  ]
}

# Expected 503 response:
#   HTTP/1.1 503 Service Unavailable
#   Retry-After: 1
#   Content-Type: application/json
#
#   {"error": "the service is temporarily at ingestion capacity; retry shortly"}
#
# Retrying the identical request after Retry-After seconds may succeed once other
# admitted-but-not-completed work has drained (unlike the 413 case in
# logs.ingest.oversized-413.rest, which can never succeed no matter when retried).
